{
  "$comment": [
    "Goodreads tags are user-created shelves, so the raw tag list is mostly library management",
    "noise: 'to-read', 'owned', 'kindle', 'read-in-2015'. This file curates the small subset that",
    "actually denotes subject matter, and folds synonyms into a canonical genre.",
    "",
    "A book's primary genre is the canonical genre with the highest summed tag count for that book.",
    "Genre matters here because it is the axis the corpus is striped along in Genre mode, and",
    "because divergent vocabulary between stripes is exactly what breaks naive score merging."
  ],
